The issue is about the model string format mismatch between what's used by aider
and the MODEL_SETTINGS in aider/models.py. The model string is like 
"claude-3-5-sonnet@20240620" (with an @ before the build identifier), but 
MODEL_SETTINGS expects a format with a hyphen instead of an at-sign before the 
build identifier like "claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620".

To fix this, I will look at the MODEL_SETTINGS dictionary in aider/models.py and
modify the logic to correctly handle the @ sign format.

First, let's inspect the MODEL_SETTINGS in aider/models.py around line 35 to 
understand its structure.

```
sed -n '30,50p' aider/models.py
```

