mini-swe-agent (step 10, $0.00):
The MODEL_SETTINGS list indeed contains ModelSettings for various Claude models 
with the build identifier separated by a hyphen, for example:

- "claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620"
- "anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620"

However, the issue pointed out that the model string coming from Vertex AI has 
an '@' symbol before the build identifier (e.g. 
"vertex_ai/claude-3-5-sonnet@20240620"). This is probably why the model never 
matches any in MODEL_SETTINGS and falls back to "whole-file editing".

To address this, I will modify the model matching logic in the place where the 
model string is compared or transformed against MODEL_SETTINGS to normalize '@' 
to '-' for the build identifier segment.

Next, I need to find where the model string is used to match against 
MODEL_SETTINGS to make this normalization. Possibly this will be in 
aider/models.py or a related file that uses MODEL_SETTINGS. I will search for 
the usage of MODEL_SETTINGS in the aider/ directory.

```
rg --json MODEL_SETTINGS aider/ --json-seq 'rg -w MODEL_SETTINGS aider/ 
--json-seq'
